// Gen III (Ruby, Sapphire, Emerald, FireRed, LeafGreen) PK3 legality through
// Legality::analyzePk3 and the production hook in Legality::analyze.
//
// Fixture records are synthetic: PKHeX.Core (commit pinned in Gen3LegalityData.h)
// built each one from its own encounter templates for a test trainer "Tester";
// the differential oracle (tools/pkhex_gen34_diff) then applied one single-field
// mutation (`generate SEED MUTATIONS 3`) or a run of ordinary play steps (`grow`).
// Expected verdict classes:
//   Valid    PKHeX VALID with no Fishy judgement other than the EXP/EV notes this
//            analyzer reports as Info: No problems found with the cartridge's id.
//   Fishy    PKHeX VALID with a Fishy judgement: Warning here, never Invalid.
//   Invalid  PKHeX INVALID and Invalid here.
//   Unknown  PKHeX INVALID only for want of save data (the e-Reader Enigma Berry):
//            Warning here, never Invalid.
// prodClean marks records Legality::analyze also certifies (the older production
// checks add no Warning of their own to them). The older Gen III checks judge the
// record's origin game and evolution lineage and yield to a certified analysis, so
// every Valid fixture is prodClean; the yield itself is tested below.
// Then constructed rule cases, malformed sizes and checksums, origin games this
// analyzer does not judge, the production merge rule, input immutability and a
// deterministic fuzz pass (ASan/UBSan under host-sanitize).
